// The Os domain: a seam on the check the client makes of every function pointer it is handed.

#ifndef WXL_SEAM_GATE
#error "define WXL_SEAM_GATE(domain, name, symbol, ret, conv, params) before including os.def"
#endif

// Ends the process with "Invalid function pointer: %p" (SErrDisplayAppFatal, error 0x85100086)
// unless the pointer lies in the executable's .text section, bounds read once by
// OsFindTextSectionBounds. The client calls it before every C function its Lua calls
// (luaD_precall, luaD_rawrunprotected), before a Lua hook (luaD_callhook), a console command's
// handler (ConsoleCommandExecute) and a CVar's callback (CVar::Set, Reset, Default and the
// array wrapper). A free function: [ebp+8] read, a bare `ret`, the callers clean: cdecl.
//
// Gated: Gate takes the call when the pointer lies in code the runtime registered (its own
// image and every binary the mod host loaded, src/runtime/Code.cpp), so a function of the
// runtime or of a mod may be handed to the client; any other pointer goes on to the client's
// check, fatal as before. It runs on every one of those calls: a pointer outside every
// registered module costs two compares.
//
// The x64 call site is in Engine/Source/Os/Win64/System.cpp. The fork's Win32 configuration
// carries no runtime: the stock 32-bit client reaches this function by detour, whose jump makes
// the client's AdditionalCheck1 (0x004046C0) skip its scan, as it does for any patch there.
WXL_SEAM_GATE(Os, ValidateFunctionPointer, "OsValidateFunctionPointer", void, cdecl, (const void* ptr))

// MSVC takes a file that expands to nothing outside its opening #ifndef X ... #endif for one
// guarded by X, and skips it when it is included again with X defined: this table is read
// several times in one translation unit, under shapes that may leave it empty. A directive
// after the rows keeps it from looking guarded.
#ifdef WXL_TABLE_END
#endif
